    summary_60s: 'The Arabic term “Caliph” is derived from the word khalīfah , meaning “successor.” In Islamic history, it refers to the leader of the Muslim community. Although the terms khalīfah and its plural khulafāʾ appear several times in the Qur’an—referring to humans as stewards or vice-re',
